              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q.5. What happens when you add up pairs of consecutive triangular numbers? That is, take 1 + 3, 3 + 6, 6 + 10, 10 + 15, … ? Which sequence do you get? Why? Can you explain it with a picture?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.148,
            0.551,
            0.166
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " We get: 4, 9, 16, 25, ……… (Square numbers)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
