            0.229,
            0.877,
            0.284
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q.6. What happens when you start to add up powers of 2 starting with 1, i.e., take 1, 1 + 2, 1 + 2 + 4, 1 + 2 + 4 + 8, …? Now add 1 to each of these numbers — what numbers do you get? Why does this happen?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.292,
            0.163,
            0.308
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans."
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.189,
            0.311,
            0.489,
            0.329
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• We get, 1, 3, 7, 15, 31, …………"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.189,
            0.33,
            0.695,
            0.366
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• After adding 1 to each number, we get:2, 4, 8, 16, 32, …… Refer the picture on page 6."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.382,
            0.866,
            0.419
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Q.7. What happens when you multiply the triangular numbers by 6 and add 1? Which sequence do you get? Can you explain it with a picture?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.428,
            0.631,
            0.502
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code_body",
              "index": 8,
              "bbox": [
                0.117,
                0.428,
                0.631,
                0.502
              ],
              "content": "Ans. (1×6) +1, (3×6) +1, (6×6) +1, (10×6) +1, (15×6) +1, …\n= 7, 19, 37, 61, 91, ….\nFor picture refer picture in Q.4 page 5."
